    "result": "Excellent! The fix is complete and verified. Let me provide a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Bug:** The `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file because the `--ci` flag was not being passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**The Root Cause:** In the `frai` CLI's `gate` command handler, Commander.js was only extracting positional arguments into the `args` parameter. The `--ci` flag (an option) was not being captured, so it wasn't forwarded to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**The Fix:** Modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-754) to use `process.argv` directly to capture all arguments after the `gate` command, rather than relying on Commander.js's parsed arguments:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n1. \u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n2. \u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed both files are created:\n   - `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n   - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` with correct GitHub Actions workflow content\n\nThe workflow file is now properly created when using the `--ci` flag through the `frai` CLI.",
